{#- Shared parts of the builtin.jkrenzer templates. The models have validated and defaulted
every value before rendering, so these templates only lay content out. A value placed inside a
list item drops its trailing line breaks (a YAML `|` block keeps one), or the blank line it
leaves would make the whole list loose; the data and its digest keep them. -#}

{% macro bullets(items) -%}
{% for item in items %}
- {{ item.rstrip("\n") | indent(2) }}
{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro references_section(references) -%}
## References and Links

{# Each reference has a designation; description and pointers are optional. Pointers are
Markdown links, bibliographic citations or precise text locations. The designation is always
followed by text or punctuation, so the item is never bold text alone (pymarkdown MD036). #}
{% for item in references %}
- **{{ item.designation }}**{% if item.description %}: {{ item.description.rstrip("\n") | indent(2) }}{% elif item.pointers %}:{% else %}.{% endif %}

{% for pointer in item.pointers %}
  - {{ pointer.rstrip("\n") | indent(4) }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
None.
{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro notes_section(notes) -%}
## Notes

{# Supplementary or administrative information belongs here. Keep requirements, decisions
and alternative evaluations in their designated sections. #}
{{ notes if notes else "None." }}
{%- endmacro %}
